Metaphysics and ontology (@metaphysics-and-ontology: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_3SNF8V7B02S3QVBRC2WVSCCZW8
Metaphysics examines what exists and how reality can be understood; ontology investigates the kinds of things an account commits us to. This material explores identity, persistence, properties, relations, parts and wholes, causation, possibility, time, reduction, and emergence. Compare ways of drawing boundaries around objects, processes, persons, and systems, explaining their assumptions and consequences. Connect these questions to physical theories, living systems, social institutions, and the abstractions used in Lince without treating a useful classification as a final division of reality.

**Parent:** [Philosophy](../Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001).
} r_3SNF8V7B02S3QVBRC2WVSCCZW8
